cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this audit framework, the 5-Gate Audit Rubric, the Case Evaluation Ledgers (Case 001 to Case 015), or the 17.37M-Line Alpöge-Claude RH/GRH Deep Decompilation & Part B AST Atlas, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Ultari Proof Anatomy: 5-Gate Technical Audit, Formal Dissection Archive & 17.37M-Line Alpöge-Claude RH/GRH Deep Decompilation"
abstract: "Byte-level zero-truncation technical audit, mathematical decompilation, and standalone Lean 4 reconstruction of frontier AI and classical mathematical formal verification corpora (v1.1.1): (1) 15 OpenAI, DeepMind, and classical case studies (892 standalone zero-sorry Lean 4 theorems, 4,217/4,217 hypothesis mutations killed across 44,833 distinct upstream .lean files, >12.4M lines) under the 5-Gate Audit Rubric, including the OpenAI #003 QRH Trilogy & Classical Riemann Barriers monograph (hexagon:2611.00912); and (2) the unified bilingual (EN/KO) deep mathematical decompilation of the 17.37M-line (175,187-file) Levent Alpöge & Claude Riemann Hypothesis (RH) and Dirichlet GRH Lean 4 archive (hexagon:2611.00881; Part A 149p EN & 134p KO deep monographs with 1,878 verified .lean:line pins each, 201/201 classical import classification [92/56/34/19], 116 Formalism subtheories [4 pillars + 112 specialized], Pure_Vwin 56 slots [50+5+1], Part B 100.00% AST Atlas across 30,343 modules and 308,731 declarations, 6-volume reader guide 55p EN & 53p KO PDFs, 195/195 literature attribution dictionary, and 61 standalone zero-sorry Lean 4 audit theorems; 953 total standalone theorems across the repository)."
